Show some sympathy.

50
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:00,720
You still find it hard to
believe that he's Ushimitsu Kozo.

51
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:01,960
It could be a lie.

52
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,800
But for right now,
that's hardly the issue.

53
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,540
It's coming back to me.

54
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,584
I could never forget that heir.

55
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:13,340
Tonoyasu is merely an alias.

56
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:16,940
What has this guy been hiding?

57
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:21,580
A lot of buzz going on
in the capital today.

58
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:22,958
I'd better tune in.

59
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,893
Someone turn on the light scroll, Snail.

60
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:39,580
Is that guy someone you know?

61
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,020
Of course he's quite famous.

62
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:49,917
Back in my day, he was a
daimyo under the Kozuki clan.

63
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,380
That's to say, he was a
close associate of Lord Odin.

64
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,760
Shimutsuki Yasui.

65
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,960
That's his name.

66
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:11,660
Sir Yasui!

67
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:24,657
the daimyo of hakumai that's
yasu the hedgehog known

68
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:27,657
for his austerity he was
famous for rarely smiling

69
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:33,717
if you can believe it even
as he stood right before

70
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:37,700
me i failed to recognize
him Stop the execution!

71
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:40,080
Olive Hakamai still loves you!

72
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:41,632
I thought you were gone!

73
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,132
Untie him, you monsters!

74
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,560
Lord Yasui!

75
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:55,140
They didn't forget about
me after all this time!

76
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,920
Ain't that sweet?

77
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:11,500
Hakumai holds a unique
position in the land of Wano,

78
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:15,100
in that it is the only region
with a legitimate port.

79
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:19,680
Some visitors wish us well,
but others wish us harm.

80
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:21,696
The course is clear.

81
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:27,960
Our army must be an unassailable force!

82
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:41,118
Without a doubt, you've got the
strongest samurai in the land of Wano.

83
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,520
Wanna buy it?

84
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:52,900
This is no time to fool
around, Odin. Wake up!

85
00:06:57,280 --> 00:07:01,517
how long are you going to loiter
here you realize that you're the son

86
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:06,517
of the shogun not some hapless vagrant
i'm afraid i was kicked out of the

87
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:12,397
castle i might have been kicked out
of the family for that matter surely

88
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:18,120
you've heard the talk people say odin will
never be heir to kozuki Hey, Sukiyaki.

89
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:23,260
Yasui will become the Shogun.

90
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:29,980
You idiot!

91
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:31,650
Ouch!

92
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,300
What was that for?

93
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,893
Don't put so much stock in idle chatter.

94
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:44,906
You're the true successor of the
Kozuki clan, beyond any doubt.

95
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:50,037
Lord Tsukiyaki only kicked you out because
he loves you and wants you to learn.

96
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:52,473
You should try to meet his expectations.

97
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,080
Maybe so.

98
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:03,180
But frankly, if I had it my
way, I'd rather go out to sea.

99
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,980
Just my luck living in a
country with closed borders.

100
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:15,580
This isolation policy is
such a pain in the ass.

101
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:21,840
Watch your mouth!

102
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:28,458
Until you're a proper samurai, you've
no right to criticize this land.

103
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:38,620
That won't hurt, you know.

104
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:41,237
You can't just keep knocking
me around like that.

105
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,614
Who do you think I am?

106
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:45,100
Right now, a nobody.

107
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,700
A mere hoodlum.

108
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:06,517
Sorry, everyone.

109
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,597
It's no use.

110
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:10,400
There's no way Orochi
is going to let me go.

111
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:16,660
First, I want to apologize for two things.

112
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:20,500
Then I'd like to say something
to that moron Orochi.

113
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:47,760
ha.

114
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:54,677
Once I get that off my chest,

115
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:58,300
I can head to the Great Beyond
with a smile on my face.

116
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:06,300
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

117
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:11,730
Attention!

118
00:10:11,813 --> 00:10:14,460
I will now read the
charges of the accused.

119
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:22,080
Last night, he was caught committing
a theft in the flower capital.

120
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:23,820
A shameless sycophant,

121
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:26,737
this former daimyo of
Hakubai has been reduced

122
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:29,900
to begging for coin as
a lowly entertainer.

123
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:33,137
His name is Shimotsuki Yasui.

124
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:38,500
He once committed the heinous crime of
rebelling against the shogun Orochi.

125
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:43,980
He will serve as an offering on this day
of the Oiran Gomorrah Saki's funeral.

126
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:48,040
We hereby sentence him
to a dishonorable death.

127
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,230
Now,

128
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:55,877
according to his statement,

129
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:59,220
he is also the serial
thief Ushimitsu Kozo,

130
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:01,637
who is a well-known public
menace in the capital.

131
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:03,700
Now that was a lie!

132
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,640
A lie?

133
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,237
But why would you say that?

134
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:13,202
Figured I might as well grab all your
attention one last time, since I'm gonna die!

135
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:16,940
I'm sorry for laughing, you guys!

136
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,965
I'm flattered you thought
I was a hero, though!

137
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:22,000
I don't understand.

138
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:26,460
Yes, it is perplexing.

139
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,437
Well, Yasui got the attention he wanted.

140
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:33,638
The uproar surrounding the Oedon's
funeral has been redirected to him.

141
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:38,290
Drake, sir!

142
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,517
The people of Evisu Town are rioting!

143
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,137
They're charging into the
flower capital in droves!

144
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:44,050
They're what?

145
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:50,060
We've made an error.

146
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:54,342
We underestimated how important
this man was to the common people.

147
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,400
Don't you go dyin' on us, Yasu!

148
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:04,140
We're coming for you, just wait!

149
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:08,693
If they don't have you to support us,
we'll be dead and rotting in a week!

150
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:11,360
Go back to Ebisu Town, you beggars!

151
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,077
You're not allowed to enter here!

152
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:13,990
Stand down!

153
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:16,970
Yasu!

154
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:26,797
The crowds on the main
street are running wild!

155
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,409
In the West District, too!

156
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:31,226
It's one thing after another.

157
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,640
In retrospect,

158
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:37,937
Lord Orochi's decision to
broadcast the execution through

159
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:41,255
the light scrolls may have
been somewhat short-sighted.

160
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:44,007
Let's keep an eye on
the other areas as well.

161
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,940
I can't help but feel sorry
for the Shogun's poor flunkies!

162
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:51,611
Must not be easy working for a damn idiot!

163
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,742
Attention, if you would, please!

164
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:08,640
Gaze upon the beauty
of the flower capital.

165
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:20,200
Our land of Wano shines brightly.

166
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:44,520
This nation is our pride and joy,

167
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:47,517
for it was won by
generations of hard work by

168
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,541
the Kozuki clan and the
people who supported them.

169
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,550
Faster!

170
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,800
Hurry up!

171
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:59,129
I don't want that bastard running
his mouth a second longer!

172
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:05,220
This is not your doing in the
least, you greedy old snake!

173
00:14:10,780 --> 00:14:14,080
You hear me, Kurosamine Orochi?

174
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:33,000
You haven't built an inch of this land.

175
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:38,480
All you've done is polluted
our fields and forests,

176
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,060
our rivers,

177
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,740
our villages.

178
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:47,800
All of their splendor has
been tainted by your greed.

179
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:52,340
You're nothing but famine.

180
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:56,060
How dare you.

181
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:06,037
I'll kill you for this
You think you can set

182
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,960
fire to my home And not
suffer the consequences

183
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:14,420
Where are you Fight me

184
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,340
Hold on

185
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,940
It can't be

186
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,260
It's all right.

187
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:37,989
You said more than enough.

188
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:40,300
Don't make the Shogun angry, please.

189
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:47,540
There's something else I should add.

190
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:51,180
Another apology while I
still have the chance.

191
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:56,760
It's about the flier with the symbol
that's been going around lately.

192
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:01,100
The Kozuki name died out 20 years ago.

193
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:04,440
I couldn't form an army
to avenge them if I tried.

194
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:07,300
But I don't want people to forget them.

195
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,560
That's why I made that flyer!

196
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:19,600
The symbol doesn't mean anything at all.

197
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:21,000
It's just a prank.

198
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:23,420
At all the cheese expense!

199
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:32,380
Oh, why would he say that?

200
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,454
There you are, Ashura.

201
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:48,920
So it's you, did you see?

202
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,240
I was shocked.

203
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:54,900
Look, at least Lord Yasui's
alive for the time being.

204
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:59,120
I saw, though I was late to
find out just as you were.

205
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:01,382
It's become quite the spectacle.

206
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:04,680
When Lord Odin died 20 years back,

207
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:09,360
Odin asked the four remaining
Damiel, including myself, a question.

208
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:15,700
Would we serve under the
Karotsumi clan or fight them?

209
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:17,960
What a laugh!

210
00:17:18,260 --> 00:17:20,920
You owed everything you had to Odin,

211
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:24,817
but you stole the Shogun's throne
out from under him with deceit.

212
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:27,800
and treachery, what fool would serve you?

213
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:33,284
The daimyo and people from every region
raised up their swords without hesitation.

214
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:38,520
But we were no match for that monster
Kaido who crushed all opposition.

215
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:41,660
And the Lamb of Wano paid the price.

216
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:46,140
Alas, I lost my chance to
die with honor in that fight.

217
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,800
So I took on a disguise and hid.

218
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:54,000
But I would be ashamed if I died
of old age, living this lie.

219
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:56,800
So, channeling my inner child,

220
00:17:57,040 --> 00:18:00,569
I came up with this flyer trick
as a final act of rebellion.

221
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:07,440
If you would forgive this
old fool, but you know,

222
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:11,380
turns out Orji was a bigger
coward than I ever imagined.

223
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:14,517
He got so spooked by the whole thing that

224
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:17,129
he jailed innocent
people just because they

225
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:21,097
followed a stylish little trend.

226
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:23,517
So it was all in his head this whole time?

227
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:24,497
What should we do?

228
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,660
We're locked away a ton of people!

229
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,740
Almost there, Lord Orochi!

230
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:35,690
Yasui!

231
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,160
You've said enough!

232
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:40,040
I'm about to pump you full of lead!

233
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:43,100
There you are!

234
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:47,140
Haven't seen you in ages, Orochi!

235
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:51,500
If you have any more last
words, save them fast!

236
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:56,537
Alright, let me see.

237
00:18:56,620 --> 00:19:01,520
Would you like me to recite
the poem that binds your heart?

238
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:12,817
A man of such small
caliber shall never know

239
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:16,980
the taste of Odin for as
long as he shall live.

240
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:38,980
Looks like this is it for me.

241
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:44,800
Kin'emon, and the rest of the
Akataya samurai, you know what to do.

242
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:49,340
And Momonosuke, I know
you'll be Shogun someday.

243
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:54,800
Your plan has not been undone.

244
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:57,040
It has merely been reset.

245
00:19:58,020 --> 00:20:01,060
Your allies in Rosetsu
Town have not been lost.

246
00:20:01,380 --> 00:20:03,860
I gave them a new rendezvous point.

247
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:13,080
It may not be much, but this is all
I can do with what's left of my life.

248
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:15,880
I feel we're helpless to stop this.

249
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:19,560
It seems he's sacrificing
himself to keep our plan alive.

250
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:23,760
There is nothing more I can say.

251
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:31,360
Thank you, my friend.

252
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:41,072
Now, no matter what that coward
or what she goes on about,

253
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:43,812
his soldiers won't listen to him anymore.

254
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:46,817
I'm getting real sick of
the Shogun's paranoia.

255
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:48,547
You can't say that out loud!

256
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:53,750
Daddy!

257
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:55,850
Yasu!

258
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:12,000
For 20 long years, we
bowed our heads in shame.

259
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:15,180
For what could we do
before the might of Kaido?

260
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:18,557
But this time, things will be different.

261
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:22,400
Cover your children's eyes! For now,

262
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:24,900
the final damio to serve Kozuki,

263
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:31,320
or rather, the happy-go-lucky fool from
Evisutown, makes his final journey!

264
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:43,590
Yasui!

265
00:21:43,673 --> 00:21:47,040
I think I'll go out singing.

266
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,560
Here we go.

267
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:57,940
Fire.

268
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:19,240
Oh, Kakarone Gashima, avenge
your lord at long last.

269
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:25,300
I shall await the good
news in the next world.

270
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:36,357
what were you thinking trying to steal
all this money lord odin was running

271
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:42,820
short on cash okay if you're gonna
kill us then do it you damn hedgehog

272
00:22:44,580 --> 00:22:48,540
what a mess where do you
find these people odin

273
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:56,680
listen up you tried to steal my
money but i'll let you keep it Huh?

274
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:00,170
Whaaaaat?

275
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:02,700
Please reconsider, Lord Yasui.

276
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:06,022
Hakumai needs those funds
much more than they do.

277
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:07,360
I don't care.

278
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:11,420
While we're at it, here's a bit more.

279
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:12,990
Take it.

280
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:15,300
Even more money?

281
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:16,873
There's a catch, right?

282
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:18,360
What is this, a trap?

283
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,940
Do you truly love Odin?

284
00:23:22,580 --> 00:23:23,900
Are you joking?

285
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:25,057
Of course we do.

286
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:26,760
I owe him my life.

287
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:28,300
Yeah, what he said.

288
00:23:29,740 --> 00:23:30,660
I see.

289
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:34,180
In that case, use this money
to clean yourselves up.

290
00:23:34,340 --> 00:23:35,280
Buy some books.

291
00:23:35,500 --> 00:23:36,680
Learn some manners.

292
00:23:37,220 --> 00:23:38,140
Get educated.

293
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:44,440
Having a bunch of unruly thugs as
vassals will only bring shame to Odin.

294
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:51,900
One day, I'm sure, he will become
the Shogun of the land of Wano.

295
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:57,074
Therefore, those who support
him must not only be loyal,

296
00:23:57,640 --> 00:24:00,580
they must be the finest
samurai in the country.

297
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:33,940
It goes without saying that
you must protect your lord.

298
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:37,720
But the people of Wano will
come to depend on you as well.

299
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:42,160
You must be a symbol of our
strength, our guardian deities.

300
00:24:42,780 --> 00:24:43,610
Understood?

301
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:46,880
Sir Yasui!

302
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,340
Daddy! Daddy!

303
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:52,300
I'm coming!

304
00:24:57,780 --> 00:24:59,040
Daddy!

305
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:03,300
Otoko.

306
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,980
I'm so sorry, Otoko.

307
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:11,060
It looks like I'll be leaving you behind.

308
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:23,510
Daddy!

309
00:25:23,593 --> 00:25:24,423
Daddy! Daddy!

310
00:25:24,506 --> 00:25:25,336
Daddy!

311
00:25:26,380 --> 00:25:27,240
Enough!

312
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:29,300
You may cease firing!

313
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,420
Yasu!

314
00:25:38,780 --> 00:25:39,640
Yasu!

315
00:25:41,660 --> 00:25:44,120
It's those beggars from Ebisu Town.

316
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:46,006
Kick them out of the capital!

317
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,240
Yosu!

318
00:25:53,580 --> 00:25:54,900
Sir Yasui!

319
00:25:57,620 --> 00:25:58,780
Nya!

320
00:25:59,060 --> 00:26:00,440
Please don't die!

321
00:26:00,940 --> 00:26:02,660
Daddy, no!

322
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:18,420
No!

323
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,310
No!

324
00:26:23,660 --> 00:26:24,490
Yasuo!

325
00:26:25,260 --> 00:26:28,280
Is that damn rat finally dead?

326
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:45,400
Lord Yasu is gone!

327
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:18,880
I don't know.

328
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:37,120
What the hell's going on here?

329
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:39,400
Yeah.

330
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:45,520
Everyone's laughing.

331
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:49,540
Somebody just died.

332
00:27:51,140 --> 00:27:54,080
Do you think that this is a joke?

333
00:28:02,660 --> 00:28:04,860
My daddy is dead!

334
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,220
You little brat!

335
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:10,560
Please, wait!

336
00:28:13,820 --> 00:28:16,880
The truth is, they are all crying.

337
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:18,940
Crying?

338
00:28:19,420 --> 00:28:23,220
The people from Ebisu
Town are always smiling.

339
00:28:23,620 --> 00:28:29,320
Because even when they're hurting or
sad, they can't show it on their faces.

340
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:55,708
Even if they're suffering, they've been
robbed of everything but their smiles.

341
00:28:57,340 --> 00:28:59,940
Now, all they can do is laugh.

342
00:29:03,540 --> 00:29:07,920
Kaido and Orochi, they
brought something here.

343
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:13,980
It's an evil fruit that they call Smile.
